### Factor Performance
Reliable factor-level realized attribution remains unavailable. The smaller loss and contained drawdown indicate improved risk control, but the ensemble was still negative. Short-horizon reversal factors remain the main implementation risk.

### Observations
- Sideways/mildly bullish conditions with elevated volatility persisted.
- Defensive tilting and volatility damping limited drawdown.
- Full-investment and long-only constraints were maintained.
- No observation-only macro instruments were traded.

### Feedback to Screener
- Continue monitoring volume-amplified and volatility-scaled reversal factors; their historical validation has not yet translated into consistently positive live performance.
- Retain momentum and peer lead-lag as core factors, while evaluating whether residual exposure adds distinct value.
- Improve factor-level PnL and turnover-cost attribution if possible.

### Plans
- Keep the 10-trading-day cadence and full-investment framework.
- Maintain the current six-factor ensemble and smoothing.
- Avoid adding further short-horizon reversal factors.
- If the next cycle remains negative, reduce aggregate reversal exposure and increase defensive stress sensitivity rather than reducing gross exposure.

